item.description:
SMAM benefit applications on SchemeApplication v0.2. One capability, ONE action: status takes the farmer's mobile or application number as SearchValue and returns SMAM's answer unchanged in commitmentAttributes -- every application, every implement and its full status history. SMAM works out for itself whether the value is a mobile or an application number, so no search type is sent.

Run Registry, Publish and Discover first, then the two Status folders. Set smam-search-value to a value SMAM holds applications for and smam-search-value-none to one it does not; both are left empty here because they are a farmer's own numbers.

